SMP PA fix: translate secondary-CPU entry/context with BootArgs (not V=P).

The kernel is NOT V=P: the SWEETXNU payload header has
virt_base=0xfffffff006000000, phys_base=0x98000000, so
    pa(va) = BootArgs->physBase + (va - BootArgs->virtBase)
and the kernel entry PA is ~0x99411488.  ml_static_vtop(&sweet_secondary_entry)
returned 0x39413800 (outside the kernel physical window), so the TZ-powered
CPU1 jumped to a random PA and died instantly; 0144's start.s "V=P" delta math
is invalid for the same reason.

  osfmk/arm64/start.s
    - sweet_secondary_entry is now address-math-free: SMCCC delivers the PSCI
      context id in x0, which the boot CPU sets to
      pa(&sweet_secondary_marks[logical]); first store
      `MOV64 x8,0x4d41524b; str x8,[x0]; dsb sy`, then a second magic
      (0x4b5241b2) to [x0,#8] after the EL branch (EL1 and EL2 paths).
      The 0144 adrp/delta macro and its marks are deleted; the remaining
      EL2/EL1 bring-up flow is unchanged and boot-CPU paths are untouched.
  osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
    - read-only sweet_get_ptov_entries() accessor (first ptov_table entries)
      for the diagnostic print; ml_static_vtop() returned a stale ptov_table
      hit instead of panicking, so its value must not be used for secondary
      CPUs on this port.
  iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
    - sweet_kva_to_pa() via BootArgs for the CPU_ON entry (x2) and context
      (x3 = PA of the mark word); prints boot virt/phys, entry_va,
      entry_vtop (ml_static_vtop), entry BootArgs PA, payload-derived entry PA,
      marks VA/vtop/PA and ptov_table[0] in the CPU_ON log and at timeout;
    - 0150's uncached mark alias uses the BootArgs translation now;
    - timeout IOLog/panic carry entry_vtop and payload PA.
  bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
    - SWEET HALT: summary now shows entry, vtop, payload and ctx.

Expected: entry BootArgs PA ~0x99411488 (payload entry 0xfffffff007411488),
ctx = PA of sweet_secondary_marks[1] (~0x9cxxxxxx), and if CPU1 runs our entry
the first word of the mark array becomes 0x4d41524b (+0x4b5241b2 at +8).
